  "details": "An editor script I have for generating VRC Triggers in worlds is getting this error with the newest SDK:\n```\n \n \n \n Assets/Worlds/Editor/TriggerGen.cs(41,18): error CS1061: 'VRC_Trigger' does not contain a definition for 'UsesAdvancedOptions' and no accessible extension method 'UsesAdvancedOptions' accepting a first argument of type 'VRC_Trigger' could be found (are you missing a using directive or an assembly reference?)\n```\n\nThe source line in question is here\n```\n    VRC_Trigger bufferTrig = gameObject.GetOrAddComponent<VRC_Trigger>();\n   \n bufferTrig.UsesAdvancedOptions = true;\n    ...\n```\nOn older SDK versions, setting `UsesAdvancedOptions=true` was required if a script generated a local trigger or otherwise requiring the Advanced checkbox to be ticked.\n\nOn newer SDK, the defaults are perfect, so the property need not do anything, but we still need that property to exist to avoid compile errors. Mark it [HideInInspector] and [Obsolete] as appropriate. Making it a no-op property setter should also work.",
